          "path": "_m/g/c/h/r/abercastle-wp/abercastell-lobsters-and-lime-.jpg",
          "filename": "Abercastell, lobsters and lime - geograph.org.uk - 917228.jpg",
          "caption": "Abercastell: lobsters and lime Abercastle was once a busy little harbour, for its size, exporting herrings and pilchards, importing coal and lime. The limekiln remains, disused, just below the coastpath here, while the modern-style pots indicate that crustaceans are still an important catch to supply local restaurants.",
