          "path": "_m/g/c/h/r/abercastle-wp/cwm-badau-bay-of-boats-abercas.jpg",
          "filename": "Cwm Badau-Bay of boats, Abercastle - geograph.org.uk - 917255.jpg",
          "caption": "Cwm Badau/Bay of boats, Abercastle Looking out to sea: mostly pleasure crafts but some fishing still goes on from the protection of this tidal haven. Although a deeply-indented inlet, the sea is shallow and ships had only a 6-hour turn-around time for loading and unloading (using horses and carts) at high tide.",
          "alt": "Cwm Badau/Bay of boats, Abercastle Looking out to sea: mostly pleasure crafts but some fishing still goes on from the protection of this tidal haven. Although a deeply-indented inlet, the sea is shallow and ships had only a 6-hour turn-around time for loading and unloading (using horses and carts) at high tide.",
          "width": 640,
          "height": 480,
          "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
          "license": "CC BY-SA 2.0",
          "artist": "ceridwen",
          "sourceUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cwm_Badau-Bay_of_boats,_Abercastle_-_geograph.org.uk_-_917255.jpg",
